\\\"Frequently asked\\\"}],null]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L6f\\\",null,{\\\"items\\\":[{\\\"q\\\":\\\"Do you need write access?\\\",\\\"a\\\":\\\"No. The review runs entirely from a read-only role you create and can delete afterwards — we supply the Terraform for it. Remediation arrives as pull requests against your infrastructure repository, which your team merges.\\\"},{\\\"q\\\":\\\"We already run a CSPM tool. What does this add?\\\",\\\"a\\\":\\\"Your CSPM tool knows configurations; it does not know which of them are reachable from an identity an attacker could get. We ingest its findings, filter out the ones that are unexploitable in your topology, and add the path analysis it cannot do. Most clients see the finding count fall sharply and the remaining list become actionable.\\\"},{\\\"q\\\":\\\"How long does the identity graph take on a large estate?\\\",\\\"a\\\":\\\"Enumeration is automated and takes hours even across dozens of accounts. The analysis is the human part: three weeks covers an estate of up to roughly 40 accounts. Beyond that we scope by business unit.\\\"},{\\\"q\\\":\\\"Can you review Kubernetes specifically?\\\",\\\"a\\\":\\\"Yes — RBAC, admission control, network policy, secrets handling, workload identity and the node-to-control-plane boundary. On managed clusters we also review the cloud identity attached to the node pool, which is where cluster compromise usually becomes account compromise.\\\"},{\\\"q\\\":\\\"Does this cover multi-cloud?\\\",\\\"a\\\":\\\"Yes, and the interesting findings are usually at the joins — the federated identity that lets a GitHub Actions workflow assume a role in AWS and a service principal in Azure, with nobody owning the trust boundary between them.\\\"},{\\\"q\\\":\\\"Will you help us fix it?\\\",\\\"a\\\":\\\"We write the infrastructure-as-code for the recommended fixes and raise them as pull requests. If you want the remediation delivered, our platform engineering practice does that as a separate engagement, and 